      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى الَّذِينَ يَمْشُونَ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ هَوْناً قَالَ هُمُ الْأَوْصِيَاءُ مِنْ مَخَافَةِ عَدُوِّهِمْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Ibn Mahboub, from Muhammad Bin Al Numan, from Sallam who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> about the Words of the Exalted <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:25#h63\"><a href=\"/books/quran:25#h63\">[25:63]</a></a> And the servants of the Beneficent are they who walk on the earth modestly</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘They<sup>asws</sup> are the successors<sup>asws</sup>, out of fear of their<sup>asws</sup> enemies’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 78. A number of our people has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn Sayf from his father from ‘Amr ibn Harith who has said the following. “I asked abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) about the words of Allah. “. . a blessed tree which has firm roots and branches rising up into the sky.” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:14#h24\"><a href=\"/books/quran:14#h24\">[14:24]</a></a> The Imam (a.s.) said that the The Holy Prophet (s.a) said, “The root is Amir al-Mu’minin Ali (a.s.) and the branches are the Imams from their (Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.) and The Holy Prophet (s.a) descendants and the knowledge of Imams stand for the fruits. Their faithful followers represent the leaves of such tree.” The Imam (a.s.) asked, “Is there anything else in the tree?” I said, “No, there is nothing else there. The Imam (a.s.) then said, “By Allah, when a faithful is given a child a leave grows in the tree and when a faithful dies a leave falls off the tree.”"
        ]
      }
